        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102389071?u=fd0b775e7e974be91ee8255925ca7b5bbbaa63f2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n  \n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Clarifies the duplicate <code class=\"notranslate\">max-age</code> headings on the <code class=\"notranslate\">Cache-Control</code> reference page by distinguishing the response and request directives. Also links the caching guide’s <code class=\"notranslate\">max-age</code><br>\nexplanation directly to the <code class=\"notranslate\">Cache-Control</code> response directive section.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Searching for <code class=\"notranslate\">max-age</code> did not surface the most relevant <code class=\"notranslate\">Cache-Control</code> response directive section clearly. Making the heading more specific and adding a direct guide link<br>\nshould help readers find the correct reference entry.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tested with:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">npx --no-install markdownlint-cli2 files/en-us/web/http/reference/headers/cache-control/index.md files/en-us/web/http/guides/caching/index.md</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">npx --no-install prettier -c files/en-us/web/http/reference/headers/cache-control/index.md files/en-us/web/http/guides/caching/index.md</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">git diff --check</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #44095.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4430303080\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44095\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44095/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44095\">#44095</a></p>\n  ",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44117",
            "title": "fix(http): clarify max-age Cache-Control sections",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-15T05:05:36.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-14T07:54:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Ashish-CodeJourney",
                "url": "https://github.com/Ashish-CodeJourney"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186039597?u=a79a9b0a67c8805cd15622ace6f73ec2cb4a1636&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a new example to the <code class=\"notranslate\">WebSocket()</code> constructor page showing how to wait for the <code class=\"notranslate\">open</code> event before calling <code class=\"notranslate\">send()</code>, and how to handle the <code class=\"notranslate\">error</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">close</code> events.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The existing examples on this page only show how to construct a <code class=\"notranslate\">WebSocket</code> and immediately close it. They don't demonstrate that the connection is asynchronous, that <code class=\"notranslate\">send()</code> must wait for the <code class=\"notranslate\">open</code> event (otherwise it throws <code class=\"notranslate\">InvalidStateError</code>), or how to handle connection failures.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This addresses the request in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2086789409\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/31768\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/31768/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/31768\">#31768</a> to clarify the connection lifecycle through working code.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The new example uses the same <code class=\"notranslate\">// Create WebSocket connection.</code> comment style as the canonical example on the parent <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebSocket\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">WebSocket</code></a> interface page, so the two examples stay consistent.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #31768.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2086789409\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/31768\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/31768/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/31768\">#31768</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44115",
            "title": "WebSocket() constructor: add event-driven example",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-14T03:58:46.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-14T03:58:25.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "TheSeydiCharyyev",
                "url": "https://github.com/TheSeydiCharyyev"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152137?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This change fixes the documentation of the LanguageDetector, Translator and Summarizer availability() static methods to reflect their specified behavior when API access is denied by Permissions Policy.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Rather than throwing a NotAllowedError or rejecting, these methods resolve with \"unavailable\".</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Specification: <a href=\"https://webmachinelearning.github.io/writing-assistance-apis/#compute-ai-model-availability\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webmachinelearning.github.io/writing-assistance-apis/#compute-ai-model-availability</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44113",
            "title": "availability() methods return \"unavailable\" when blocked",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-13T18:05:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-13T18:03:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "reillyeon",
                "url": "https://github.com/reillyeon"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58849388?u=08f6cc6d91f53b66e6fce613311b6868aa6f16cf&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a focused section to the WebExtensions <code class=\"notranslate\">background</code> manifest documentation explaining how a Manifest V3 extension can specify both <code class=\"notranslate\">background.scripts</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">background.service_worker</code> for cross-browser background behavior.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The update also clarifies that <code class=\"notranslate\">background.preferred_environment</code> is not required for the basic fallback behavior, and should only be used when an extension specifically wants to prefer a service worker where available.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #44100.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4433445950\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44100\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44100/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44100\">#44100</a>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Validation</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">npx --yes prettier@3.8.3 --check \"files/en-us/mozilla/add-ons/webextensions/manifest.json/background/index.md\"</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">npx --yes --package markdownlint-cli2@0.22.1 --package markdownlint-rule-search-replace@1.2.0 markdownlint-cli2 \"files/en-us/mozilla/add-ons/webextensions/manifest.json/background/index.md\"</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">git diff --check</code></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44108",
